    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nbase16\n\n### Description\n\nIn my previous issue (#171), @echasnovski suggested:\r\n> At the moment, I am inclined to let the user fine-tune tree-sitter highlight groups by manually defining them. But I'll think about this more.\r\n\r\nThis issue is a continuation of that discussion, as I have noticed another unexpected change in the colorscheme and wanted to formalise your suggestion as a feature request :)\r\n\r\nA [recent treesitter update](https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter/commit/7ce62670b2e0946e3f586f3f07a584f642b02b9b?diff=split) moved the keywords related to storage class into the `@storageclass` and `@type.qualifier` highlight groups (linked to the builtin `StorageClass` and `Type` groups respectively). This change has the unfortunate effect of making C code look quite green:\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/25364469/206439563-ed27008d-763e-49c3-b719-09d3cac83b60.png)\r\n\r\nFor a slightly less contrived example, function return types are a bit more difficult to see at a glance:\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/25364469/206442358-2b4d1fa1-b095-4728-b996-4cad069e7a10.png)\r\n\r\nSince treesitter is quite unstable, and changes such as this are common and difficult to track, the implementation of this feature would allow users to change the colours back to how they were without the plugin requiring an update every time a group is changed.\r\n\r\nFor example, using `hi! link @storageclass Keyword` and `hi! link @type.qualifier Keyword` to simulate overriding these groups would allow users to revert the change themselves:\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/25364469/206443482-68bbf57b-7e66-4356-a5f6-d35440c70e89.png)\r\n\r\nSince these changes are likely to continue until treesitter stabilises, this feature is an interim solution.",
